tes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Equatorial","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Ecliptic","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/EclipticState","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Horizon","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Spherical","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Vector3D","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/StateVector","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/RotationMatrix","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Refraction"]},{"title":"Time","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime"],"anchor":"Time"},{"title":"Configuration","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyConfig","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/DeltaTModel"],"anchor":"Configuration"},{"title":"Errors","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError"],"anchor":"Errors"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"AstronomyKit-logo","type":"image"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstronomyKit wraps Don Cross’s "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/cosinekitty\/astronomy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and exposes the underlying C functionality through idiomatic Swift APIs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Features","text":"Features","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions for the Sun, Moon, planets, and Jupiter’s moons"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ecliptic position and velocity in one call: longitude, latitude, distance, and their rates"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Moon phase angles, quarter searches, illumination, and libration"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sunrise, sunset, moonrise, culmination, and custom altitude searches"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lunar and solar eclipse prediction with timing","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Equinoxes and solstices for any year","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Transforms between equatorial, ecliptic, horizontal, and galactic frames","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Full ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" conformance for Swift 6","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Quick-Start","text":"Quick Start","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import AstronomyKit","","\/\/ Your location","let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7128, longitude: -74.0060)  \/\/ NYC","","\/\/ Current moon phase","let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","print(\"\\(Moon.emoji(for: angle)) \\(Moon.phaseName(for: angle))\")","","\/\/ Next sunrise","if let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Sunrise: \\(sunrise.date)\")","}","","\/\/ Where is Mars?","let mars = try CelestialBody.mars.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","print(\"Mars: \\(mars.altitude)° \\(mars.compassDirection)\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Planetary evaluation","anchor":"Planetary-evaluation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Qualified segments from 1900 through 2100 TT use compiled polynomial approximations of the full VSOP87B model. Position and heliocentric velocity share one representation. Dates outside that interval and unqualified segments use the full series, so the supported date range is unchanged. The tables add about 11.5 MB before platform packaging.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Numerical compatibility","anchor":"Numerical-compatibility","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstronomyKit uses platform-native math. Linux is supported with the same astronomical accuracy tests. Results may differ slightly across platforms, architectures, OS releases, toolchains, and build configurations; cross-platform bit identity is not guaranteed. Event-time calculations can amplify these rounding differences."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For persisted numerical caches, include ","type":"text"},{"code":"AstronomyConfig.ephemerisVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the platform, architecture, OS, and toolchain identity. Review stored positions and event times when upgrading. Numerical regression tolerances are separate from absolute astronomical accuracy limits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit"]}],"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/CoordinateSystems":{"title":"Coordinate Systems","abstract":[{"text":"Transform positions between different astronomical coordinate systems.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CoordinateSystems","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/coordinatesystems","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/Sun":{"title":"Sun","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/sun","abstract":[{"text":"Contains functions for calculating Sun position and related values.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sun","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Sun","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Sun","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/MoonPhases":{"abstract":[{"text":"Calculate moon phases, quarters,